  <!--
    This project links the application's whole-program-optimized objects, and a
    listing option recorded in an object still applies when the linker generates
    that object's code.  So this link writes the same sakura_core listings that
    sakura.vcxproj writes, and it hits the same collision: code generation is
    partitioned by function, so two threads holding functions from one source
    file open one .asm and the second open fails the Win32 share check, reported
    as "C1083 ... Permission denied" plus LNK1257.  Serialize code generation
    under the same opt-in switch that produces the listings.
  -->
